{
 "verdicts": {
  "1_BKPV_FJ": "Sign identical on both sides (m_c down 0.36 / up 0.17 at 1 sigma; V1 DIAGNOSIS dmc convention). Difference is entirely the asymmetric-error convention: production = continuous two-piece normal (mode at centre, side masses 68:32, mean -0.152) + M_h 0.053; blind = equal-mass split (median at centre, 16/84% points, mean -0.076). Blind integrator with production convention: 0.6235 (production 0.6258; residual = main-value offset 0.002). Production is internally inconsistent (its model-error asymmetry uses equal-mass Gauss-Hermite z-scaling; BKPV/FJ and measurements use two-piece). Recommendation: pick one convention for all; quote BKPV/FJ variant 0.63-0.67 with the convention stated.",
  "2_HLLHC": "dm_t inputs equivalent (YR 1902.04070 Table 47 pdf p.149: 0.17 GeV; Corcella 1903.06574 pdf p.13 rounds the same CMS projection to 'about 0.2 GeV'). The difference is delta alpha_s: production keeps 0.0009 (alpha_s term 0.348 of sigma_tot 0.423 -> 1.66 sigma, reproduced by blind integrator 1.655); blind used 0.0002, which YR pdf p.88 states is an assumed future lattice-QCD precision, not an HL-LHC measurement. FCC FSR pdf p.97: lattice-dominated world average expected to improve by x2 in a decade (~0.00045) -> 2.4-2.5 sigma, the most defensible HL-LHC-era central value; 0.0002 gives 2.8-3.1 sigma (optimistic); with MC-pole interpretation 0.5 retained ~1.2 sigma. Recommend '1.7 sigma (alpha_s unchanged) to 2.4 sigma (lattice x2)', state the alpha_s premise; the HL-LHC gain is almost entirely from alpha_s.",
  "3_hLb_slope": "Same variable: D124 row (4) uses eta_inf ~ 1/hL_b at fixed mu_b, identical to T17's ln eta. D124's 'per e-fold' = one-sided secant for eta x e (-0.170/-0.270/-0.394), reproduced on the C149 curve (-0.1703/-0.2697/-0.3938); eta/e gives +0.214/+0.367; tangent (T17, blind +-10%) = -0.189/-0.310/-0.471. The 11-16% difference is the concavity of ln I(m_t) (slope 5.3 -> 2.1 /GeV). Both correct; use tangent for small variations, symmetric secant or the asymmetric pair for full e-folds.",
  "extra_bayes_prior": "Production flat_150_200 prior is effectively flat on [160,186] (indicator on the Theory2 grid mg, C154_core_v2.py l.343-348): prior mean 0.498 vs correct 0.459; B_selection(direct,[150,200]) should be 1.584 (not 1.459), B_selection_max 2.18 (not 2.007). B_existence and [170,176] unaffected."
